The builder, the scripts, the configs, the tests and the documentation are MIT.
The DATA is not, and MIT must not be read as a grant over it. Each dataset
subset carries the licence of its source corpus, and they differ:

  - tr_intent, en_intent (+paired)  CC-BY-4.0
  - vitamins_tr, musteri_tr,
    sinema_tr                       CC-BY-SA-4.0  (SHARE-ALIKE, contagious)
  - marc_en                         Apache-2.0
  - amazon_hpc_en                   no licence; text withheld, rebuilt locally
  - sikayet_tr, interpress_tr       no licence; text withheld, rebuilt locally
                                    (licence enquiry open with the upstream
                                     rights holders -- see DATACARD.md)

Anything derived from a share-alike subset must stay CC-BY-SA-4.0. The three
withheld sets ship as questions and answers only. See DATACARD.md for the full
position and the reasoning behind it.

